  ],
  "summary": {
    "keyInsights": [
      "$\\sin(2\\theta) = \\frac{24}{25}$ using double angle formula $\\sin(2\\theta) = 2\\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta)$"
    ],
    "fullSolution": "From $\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{3}{5}$: $\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{4}{5}$ (3-4-5 triangle). Then $\\sin(2\\theta) = 2(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{4}{5}) = \\frac{24}{25}$",
